; ohtomo_type_a.cnl — a redrawn Type-A (two-device parallel) amplifier, the topology of
; M. Ohtomo, "Stability Analysis and Numerical Simulation of Multidevice Amplifiers",
; IEEE Trans. MTT vol. 41 no. 6/7, 1993, and the circuit the 2025 envelope paper sweeps.
;
; Two identical devices are driven in parallel from one input node and combined at one output
; node. The EVEN mode is what the amplifier is for; the ODD mode — the two devices in antiphase —
; sees the input and output nodes as virtual grounds and closes a loop through the two gates that
; nothing in the matching network damps. Rb across the gates is the balancing resistor that damps
; it, and it is the element the whole analysis is about: at Rb = 30 Ohm this circuit is stable at
; 50 Ohm, and at Rb = 100 Ohm the odd mode starts up at 6.09 GHz. Because the odd mode sees both
; ports as virtual grounds, NO source or load termination reaches it — which is why the fixture is
; also the demonstration that a source/load stability ENVELOPE cannot see an odd-mode instability.
;
; Redrawn with circuitRF's own element values (overview D-15): no vendor kit, no part number,
; no figure copied. The device is an eleven-element small-signal FET written out of primitives —
; Rg, Ri, Cgs, Cgd, Cds, Rds, gm, and the gate/drain line inductances beside it — which is what
; an eleven-element FET model is.
;
;   PS (idx 1) sits DIRECTLY at the source Term, G facing it — the envelope's source probe;
;   PG (idx 2) is the suspect probe, in device 1's gate node, where the odd mode lives;
;   PL (idx 3) sits directly at the load Term, L facing it — the envelope's load probe.
; (idx is flattened netlist order, so it follows the order the three are WRITTEN below.)
;
; Passivating for the NDF is `G=0.40` -> `G=0` on both VCCS: the NDFgm pattern of WSP-6.
Term:T1     p1 0    Num=1 Z=50 Ohm
WSProbe:PS  p1 in
L:LIN1  in g1    L=0.25 nH
L:LIN2  in g2    L=0.25 nH
R:RB    g1 g2    R=30 Ohm

; ── device 1 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WSProbe:PG  g1 g1a
R:RG1   g1a gi1  R=0.5 Ohm
C:CGS1  gi1 s1   C=0.50 pF
C:CGD1  gi1 d1   C=0.45 pF
VCCS:M1 d1 s1  gi1 s1  G=0.40
R:RDS1  d1 s1    R=1000 Ohm
C:CDS1  d1 s1    C=0.08 pF
L:LS1   s1 0     L=0.10 nH

; ── device 2 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
R:RG2   g2 gi2   R=0.5 Ohm
C:CGS2  gi2 s2   C=0.50 pF
C:CGD2  gi2 d2   C=0.45 pF
VCCS:M2 d2 s2  gi2 s2  G=0.40
R:RDS2  d2 s2    R=1000 Ohm
C:CDS2  d2 s2    C=0.08 pF
L:LS2   s2 0     L=0.10 nH

; ── output combiner ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
L:LO1   d1 out   L=0.40 nH
L:LO2   d2 out   L=0.40 nH
WSProbe:PL  out p2
Term:T2     p2 0    Num=2 Z=50 Ohm
analysis SP1 type=sparam start=0.2 stop=20 npts=991 Unit=GHz
